POWER BI PROJECT DOCUMENTATION

Project Overview

This document describes the scope, dataset, analytical dimensions, key performance indicators, and business questions for the Sales Performance Dashboard project. It is intended to guide the development of an interactive Power BI dashboard.

1. Project Title

Sales Performance Dashboard Using Power BI

2. Project Introduction

The Sales Performance Dashboard is a data analytics and visualization project developed using Microsoft Power BI. The project focuses on analyzing Superstore sales data to understand overall business performance.

The dashboard provides insights into sales, profit, product categories, customer segments, geographical performance, and shipping methods. Using interactive charts, graphs, KPI cards, and filters, users can explore sales trends and identify areas that may require improvement.

3. Problem Statement

Businesses generate large amounts of sales data every day. However, analyzing this data manually can be time-consuming and makes it difficult to identify important business trends and performance issues.

The objective of this project is to transform raw Superstore sales data into meaningful visual insights using Power BI. The dashboard helps identify profitable products, high-performing regions, customer purchasing patterns, and areas where sales or profitability need improvement.

4. Project Objectives

Analyze overall sales and profit performance.

Identify the best-performing product categories and subcategories.

Understand sales performance across different geographical regions.

Analyze customer segments and their purchasing behavior.

Identify the most profitable products and customers.

Evaluate shipping methods and their relationship with sales.

Analyze monthly and yearly sales trends.

Build an interactive dashboard using Power BI.

Support better business decisions through data-driven insights.

5. Dataset Description

The project uses the Superstore Sales Dataset, which contains transactional sales information from a retail business. The dataset includes information about customer orders, product categories, sales amounts, profits, discounts, shipping details, and geographical locations.

