7. Business Dimensions

Business dimensions are the categories used to organize and analyze sales data from different perspectives.

Dimension

Description

Time Dimension

Analysis by order date, month, quarter, and year.

Product Dimension

Analysis by category, subcategory, and product.

Customer Dimension

Analysis by customer name and segment.

Geographical Dimension

Analysis by country, state, city, and region.

Shipping Dimension

Analysis by shipping mode and shipping date.

8. Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)

The following KPIs will be used to monitor the business's sales performance:

KPI

Description

Total Sales

Total revenue generated.

Total Profit

Total profit earned.

Total Orders

Number of unique orders.

Total Quantity Sold

Total number of units sold.

Average Order Value

Average sales value per unique order.

Profit Margin (%)

Percentage of sales converted into profit.

Average Discount

Average discount applied across transactions.

Suggested DAX Measures

Assuming the imported Power BI table is named Orders:

Total Sales

Total Sales = SUM(Orders[Sales])

Total Profit

Total Profit = SUM(Orders[Profit])

Total Orders

Total Orders = DISTINCTCOUNT(Orders[Order ID])

Total Quantity

Total Quantity = SUM(Orders[Quantity])

Average Order Value

Average Order Value = DIVIDE([Total Sales], [Total Orders])

Profit Margin

Profit Margin = DIVIDE([Total Profit], [Total Sales]) * 100

Average Discount

Average Discount = AVERAGE(Orders[Discount])

Note: Replace Orders with the actual table name if your imported dataset uses a different name. Format Profit Margin as a percentage in Power BI; if the measure is formatted as Percentage, remove the * 100 from the formula.

9. Business Questions

What is the total sales and profit generated by the business?

Which product category generates the highest sales?

Which product subcategory generates the highest profit?

Which geographical region performs best in terms of sales?

Which customer segment contributes the most revenue?

Who are the top 10 customers based on sales?

Which products generate the highest and lowest profits?

How do sales and profits change over time?

Which shipping method is most frequently used?

How do discounts affect overall profitability?

Which states generate the highest sales?

Are there any products or regions generating negative profits?

